<article class="env-lemma" id="037S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037S">Lemma <span data-tag="037S">10.48.2</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $R$ be a $k$-algebra. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for every field extension $k'/k$ the spectrum of $R \otimes _ k k'$ is connected, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every finite separable field extension $k'/k$ the spectrum of $R \otimes _ k k'$ is connected. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For any extension of fields $k'/k$ the connectivity of the spectrum of $R \otimes _ k k'$ is equivalent to $R \otimes _ k k'$ having no nontrivial idempotents, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00EF" data-tag="00EF">10.21.4</a>. Assume (2). Let $k \subset \overline{k}$ be a separable algebraic closure of $k$. Using Lemma <a href="/tag/00I3" data-tag="00I3">10.43.4</a> we see that (2) is equivalent to $R \otimes _ k \overline{k}$ having no nontrivial idempotents. For any field extension $k'/k$, there exists a field extension $\overline{k}'/\overline{k}$ with $k' \subset \overline{k}'$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/037R" data-tag="037R">10.48.1</a> we see that $R \otimes _ k \overline{k}'$ has no nontrivial idempotents. If $R \otimes _ k k'$ has a nontrivial idempotent, then also $R \otimes _ k \overline{k}'$, contradiction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>